## Lore

The cities of the Ishpeming Republic need a force for urban crime and city defense, so Ishpeming keeps its traditional Police Department (IPD), staffed by residents born, raised and living in the Republic rather than by mercs. The IPD concentrates on peacekeeping, protecting NG citizens and bringing murderers, violent criminals and anyone threatening Northern Gun''s profits to justice. Because the corporate hierarchy overlooks many minor crimes, it has a high proportion of detectives and SWAT-style tactical officers, plus highway patrol on Police rocket bikes and beat cops, all used to perpetrators augmented with cybernetics, M.O.M., Juicer technology or magic. They also patrol the IM Highway from Ishpeming to Manistique.

At Northern Gun the police are respected defenders of the law-abiding citizens against the rude, crude and scary visitors from the outside world. The IPD works closely with the Loss Prevention Office and mercenary groups. It normally sticks to Ishpeming/Northern Gun, Marquette and the surrounding cities; Escanaba is policed by the mercenary company known as the Patrol.

Officers work four 10-12 hour days, have three days off, work eight days in a row, have six off and repeat, and may freelance on their time off. A player character may also be a retired NG Police Officer turned private detective, security specialist, bodyguard or troubleshooter.

Alignment: Any, though most are Principled (30%), Scrupulous (40%) or Unprincipled (10%); dirty cops are likely Anarchist or evil. Only humans officially serve in the IPD; D-Bees and magic users are relegated to confidential informants or special contractors.

## Equipment

All IPD: street uniform, dress uniform, NG 122-EXO Light Police Power Armor (or any light or medium Northern Gun M.D.C. body armor in police colors and logo), police badge/I.D., citation book, headset radio, pocket computer, laser distancer, 2 sets of M.D.C. handcuffs, 1D4x10 zip ties (2D4 S.D.C.), extendable baton (2D4 S.D.C. damage), S.D.C. pistol of choice with 4 extra clips, and a Northern Gun energy rifle and energy pistol of choice with 4 extra E-Clips for each.

Crisis Response Officer: Mantis, Defender, Juicer Killer or Samson power armor; on foot, NG 122-EXO Light Police Power Armor or other NG medium or heavy body armor, sniper rifles and heavier weapons like plasma ejectors and particle beam rifles. The NG-GL10 grenade launcher is popular, as are tear gas and stun grenades. Patrol hover cars, Crisis Response Vehicles, tanks and robots are available by assignment.

Highway Patrol: NG 122-EXO Light Police Power Armor and the Police NG Interceptor Rocket Bike as standard; some prefer the NG Turbo, Streetrunner or Jouster hovercycles. Red Hawk power armor, Sky King aircraft and jet packs are also used.

Investigator: a field computer with access to Northern Gun''s customer and criminal database, a crime scene investigation kit, and an Urban Patrol Hovercar on duty; uniforms from other NG departments for going unnoticed.

Undercover Agent: a small side arm like the NG Holdout ion pistol and a Vibro-Blade of choice; equipment, disguises, vehicles and cash as each assignment needs; a hovercycle, motorcycle, hovercraft or jet pack for field work.

## Pay and cybernetics

Average salary is 6,000 credits per month; inspectors and officers ranked sergeant or above make 8,000.

Cybernetics: none to start. Some officers have eye-cameras, radios, clock-calendars, augmented hearing, molecular analyzers, vital-signs monitors, tracking beacons and other job-related implants.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ng-police-officer');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ng-police-officer';

